.nh
.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
orbit-release-check - Watch the release-tier check, or run the release tier against the local dev services


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit release check [repo] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Without --local, polls the open release pull request's checks until two consecutive polls report the same complete set. Exit 0 means pass, 1 means failure, 2 means no release pull request or no checks. With --local, creates a throwaway database in the existing dev Postgres, runs the repository's release tier against the dev Postgres, Redis and NATS, and drops the database in every case. It starts no containers.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for check

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Print the result as a JSON envelope

.PP
\fB--local\fP[=false]
	Run the release tier against the existing dev Postgres, Redis and NATS

.PP
\fB--wait-timeout\fP=20m0s
	Maximum time to wait for release checks


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file

.PP
\fB--manifest\fP=""
	Path to workspace.yaml


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBorbit-release(1)\fP
